@h1 Faceted content h1@

One source, many gated views — a draft with editorial notes and a clean final, a
public edition and an internal one, a build per target. Wit does this with data
flags, conditionals, and multiple build roots. This page covers the verified
path and, honestly, the two things people reach for that do not exist.

@h2 The verified path h2@

Model each facet as @strong data strong@ and gate content on it with a
conditional:

@@@pre
#doc: { audience - public, status - draft }

(if @doc.status is draft)
  @aside Editorial: tighten this section. aside@
(end)

(if @doc.audience is internal)
  @section Internal appendix: raw figures. section@
(end)
pre@@@

Flip the flag in @@@code #doc code@@@ and the gated blocks appear or vanish. You
can also iterate over annotated sections and gate each, and use @code ~ code@
line comments for scratch notes that never render at all.

@h2 Membership without contains h2@

There is @strong no strong@ @code contains code@ operator. To model membership —
"is this in the internal set?" — compare a single flag with @code is code@ or
@code equals code@, or keep one flag per facet:

@@@pre
#doc: { public - true, internal - false }

(if @doc.public) … visible in the public build … (end)
pre@@@

For anything richer, filter in a @@@code <% %> code@@@ script.

@h2 Build roots, not conditional references h2@

To ship genuinely different @strong subsets of files strong@, use @strong
multiple build roots strong@ — a small master per edition, each referencing the
files that edition includes. What you @strong cannot strong@ do is wrap a
@@@code reference code@@@ in an @@@code (if) code@@@: conditional references are
not supported (see @a |href /docs/guides/multi-file/| Multi-file references a@).
Choose the build root instead.

@aside(class note) 💡 Per-target dispatch — rendering differently for HTML vs slides — lives in a @@@code <% %> code@@@ script through a renderer-provided target value, not in the core language. Cross-link @a |href /docs/guides/derived-content/| Derived content a@. aside@

@h2 Common mistakes h2@

@ul
@li Reaching for @code contains code@ — model membership as a flag compared with
@code is code@ / @code equals code@. li@
@li Wrapping a @@@code reference code@@@ in an @@@code (if) code@@@ — pick a build
root per edition. li@
ul@

